  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICMPS BANGKOK 2021-MAE TAO CLINIC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide HIV screening to pregnant women, babies born within the prevention of mother-to-child transmission (PMTCT) programme, blood donors, partners of people living with HIV, and patients with sexually transmitted infections (STIs) for HIV. Patients will also be counselled and tested when they come for voluntary testing or when medics find medical indicators that suspect HIV. As a result of this programme, people living with HIV (PLHA) will have access to indispensable medical care in need and result in the reduced rate of HIV transmission in the target communities. MTC refers HIV-positive patients to Myawaddy Hospital in order for them to access ART. MTC facilitates these patients&#x2019; enrolment in Myanmar&#x2019;s national HIV programme by providing a peer who can accompany new patients to Myawaddy so they can get familiar with the system.</narrative>
  </description>
